content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 C and rising. The manual limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is 2 C above the trip limit, so the pump must be stopped. Temperatures are measured on the housing surface, which matches how the reading was taken.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 4.0 mm/s. On Figure 3 this falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). That is acceptable on its own but only 0.5 mm/s below the Zone C 'Restricted – plan maintenance' boundary. This assumes the value is RMS velocity and is the highest of the two bearing-housing readings, as the monitoring procedure requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drive-end bearing is reported as noisy. The manual requires replacing both bearings as a pair when either shows noise or high temperature, and both conditions are present.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. This is the most likely cause: the bearing is noisy and over-temperature, and bearing wear is listed under both high bearing temperature and high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed under both high bearing temperature and high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the bearing. It is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-110 immediately, because the bearing temperature of 92 C exceeds the 90 C trip limit. Then isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the bearing housings for over-greasing and record the findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: the drive-end bearing HF3-512 (6312-C3) and the non-drive-end bearing HF3-510 (6310-C3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly has to be removed, use lifting equipment because it weighs 68 kg. Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. Tighten the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm and the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm, with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the mechanical seal is disturbed, follow SB-2026-014 because this pump is serial HF3-24020, which is at or above HF3-22000. Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, and tighten the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not 25 Nm. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 and replace it if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm, with lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out a laser shaft alignment, since the bearing housing has been worked on. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the Plan 11 seal flush from the pump discharge is in place, and never run the pump dry. After restart, check that bearing housing temperature stays at or below the 70 C normal limit. Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3, aiming for Zone A or B.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replaced as a pair with the drive-end bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket – required only if the casing is opened or the back pull-out assembly is removed",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above) – required only if the seal is disturbed",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Do not continue running the pump: the bearing housing temperature of 92 C is above the 90 C trip limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before any dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the seal has to be replaced, add mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "For the mechanical seal part, the manual parts list (Rev D) gives HF3-450, a component-type seal. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with HF3-450B for HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial HF3-24020 is in that range, so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the seal gland nut torque, manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because serial HF3-24020 is at or above HF3-22000, 30 Nm applies. Table 5 still applies to all other fasteners on this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Manual section 5.2 step 4 requires inspecting the sleeve. The bulletin states HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting, but the sleeve must be replaced if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. The bulletin applies to this serial number.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The manual gives no step-by-step bearing replacement procedure. It does not say whether the back pull-out assembly or the mechanical seal must be removed to change the bearings, so it is not confirmed whether the gasket and seal will be needed.",
    "The evidence does not specify grease type, grease quantity or relubrication interval, so the over-greasing check cannot be measured against a limit.",
    "The report does not state whether the 4.0 mm/s vibration is RMS velocity, or whether it is the highest reading of the two bearing housings, as required for Figure 3 classification.",
    "No lockout or isolation procedure, hot-surface precautions or PPE requirements are given in the evidence beyond 'isolate and drain'.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing temperature and the pump's recent operating history (flow, NPSH, recent greasing) are not reported."
  ]
}
